pproval:<id> and done-when:<id> Adjudicates tokens; it composes each named class through compose with that section's verdict path in fixed amendment, first-approval, done-when order, and refuses whole if any section cannot compose. Its verdict is checked against the kinds requested by its composed brief: it refuses no requested kinds, a different SITTING: JUDGED kind list, or anything other than exactly one kind-form lower-case heading per requested kind and no other kind-form heading; each section passes that class's grammar. The Done-when holds use this same validator and accept a Done-when line only from a valid verdict and its own section. Token and section parsing are shared by composition, validation, act scopes and merge-time minting; the class is routed and retainable through BRIEF_PROMPTS.\"","+module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/adjudicate_brief.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/sitting.py;project-trajectory/scripts/coordinator_adjudicate.py\"","+code_symbol = \"requested_kinds/_sitting_scopes/combined_values;scopes/sections/own_section/brief_scope/GRAMMAR/DONE_WHEN_OUTCOMES/line_refusal/named_kinds/sitting_refusal/parse/requested_path/render_requested/read_requested/REQUESTED_SUFFIX;bind_requested\"","+detail = \"A combined class accepts only amendment:<id>, first-approval:<id> and done-when:<id> Adjudicates tokens; it composes each named class through compose with that section's verdict path in fixed amendment, first-approval, done-when order, and refuses whole if any section cannot compose. One parser reads a verdict into its kind lines: a combined sitting names exactly the kinds bound at reservation in <verdict>.requested, has exactly one kind-form lower-case section per bound kind and none other, and has exactly one complete own-kind machine line in each section; a single-kind verdict has no kind-form section and exactly one complete machine line. The coordinator verdict check and Done-when holds consume that parse, so an unbound combined verdict covers nothing. Token and section parsing are shared by composition, validation, act scopes and merge-time minting; the class is routed and retainable through BRIEF_PROMPTS.\""," rationale = \"A shared checkpoint reduces adjudication launches only if no constituent judgement loses its scope or grammar. One parser prevents composition, validation and later acts from interpreting the same sitting differently.\""," test_refs = \"TC-327\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-841\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":2684,"oldLines":7,"newStart":2684,"newLines":7,"lines":[" [test.TC-257]"," verifies = [\"SR-154\", \"SR-156\", \"LLR-262\", \"IF-242\"]"," level = \"Integration\"","-method = \"On git repositories, in modules registered as slow: a later commit rewriting a CHANGES-REQUESTED round to APPROVE, asserted to leave the governing identity unmoved, leaves the gate refusing; a verdict its logged session never committed is no round; a later session that commits a verdict-only rewrite and then rewrites the earlier session log to name that clean range is refused by name at the merge ladder, naming the log and the commit that modified it, and the gate does not clear; the merge ladder refuses by name, naming the session log and each path, a review range that changed files beside its verdict, through the ladder itself, and passes a clean one. Driving the loop with a fake agent: a clean review is accepted; a reviewer committing a file beside its verdict stops the run needing a human and names the file; a reviewer leaving an untracked file fails its draw, the same phase re-drawn on another reviewer completes the round and the file is stashed under a named entry, while a stash that fails - driven through the loop with the reviewer holding the index lock - stops the run needing a human with the paths named after exactly one review launch, and, called directly, neither cools the route nor arms a r