{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfnMVmcGdStsbHCnuvPXX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All seven amended rows change meaning (`VERDICT: MEANING rows=7`). I'd bless each new text, so I re-attested all seven.\n\nThe design behind them: the coordinator records what a sitting was asked to judge in a `.requested` file beside its verdict. One parser then judges every verdict against that record, both when validating it and when deciding whether it releases a hold.\n\n- **LLR-306:** the entry point now creates that binding exclusively before launch. It refuses if the binding already exists or can't be written, removes the binding along with the reservation on a pre-launch refusal, and commits the binding in its own telemetry commit.\n- **LLR-307 and LLR-310:** a combined sitting is judged against the bound kinds, not the kinds it states itself. A sitting with no binding releases nothing. A single-kind verdict must have no kind sections and exactly one complete machine line.\n- **LLR-308:** the done-when verdict needs exactly one complete DONE-WHEN line. A second line, even an incomplete one, now gets the verdict refused.\n- **TC-257:** \"a covered change mints none\" becomes \"mints no goalposts adjudication\". That lets a SUCCESSOR verdict's own drafts be minted, which matches LLR-262.\n- **TC-326 and TC-327:** they add the matching tests: an incomplete second line, a sitting with no binding, a missing requested kind, a properly bound sitting that does release, and the entry-point binding itself.\n\n**Why I'd bless them:** the code in `415ac6a8` matches (`bind_requested` and `_release` in `coordinator_adjudicate.py`, plus the `.requested` reader), and the cited tests check exactly these cases.\n\n**Commits:**\n- `268e4ed5` — the verdict file `011-ADJUDICATE-c1d8dc6.md`, with the trailer `WI: WI-841`.\n- `a91e8c81` — the re-attestation: `intake.py snapshot --reattests` naming all seven rows, which copied both registries and recorded act seq 51 in the act ledger.\n\nThe snapshot wasn't refused, so nothing else in either registry has drifted. The pre-commit checks passed on both commits.\n\n**For the coordinator:** `011-ADJUDICATE-c1d8dc6.md.requested`, the binding for this sitting, is still untracked. I left it alone because LLR-306 says the coordinator commits it in its own telemetry commit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":713,"cache_read_input_tokens":317879,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":713},"output_tokens":725,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2cffbbc6-0175-4e90-b9ab-7b165e0c0246","uuid":"7549c5aa-89da-4e4f-8010-a9da4bea602f","timestamp":"2026-10-07T05:51:05.033Z","request_id":"req_011CfnMVmDTigg7xYPYxjLLD"}
